```cpp
uint32_t* createNeighborTable(
    Particle *sortedParticles, const size_t &particleCount)
{
    // Allocate and initialize the table with NO_PARTICLE
    uint32_t *table = new uint32_t[TABLE_SIZE];
    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < TABLE_SIZE; i++) {
        table[i] = NO_PARTICLE;
    }

    // Iterate through sorted particles and record first index for each hash
    for (size_t i = 0; i < particleCount; i++) {
        uint16_t hash = sortedParticles[i].hash;
        // Only set if not already set (first particle with this hash)
        if (table[hash] == NO_PARTICLE) {
            table[hash] = static_cast<uint32_t>(i);
        }
    }

    return table;
}
```

Since particles are sorted by hash, the first occurrence of each hash value marks the beginning of that hash's particle range in the sorted array. The table stores these starting indices, allowing quick lookup of all particles sharing the same cell hash.

